  "descriptionMarkdown": "# Input/Output\nInput from the top, left to right:\n1. [item=jellynut] Jellynut: 230/min\n2. [item=yumako] Yumako: 577/min\n3. [fluid=water] Water: 0.2 pumps\n\nOutput to the left:\n\n[item=agricultural-science-pack] Agricultural science packs: 355-360/min\n\n# Usage\n\n* Connect inputs. The [entity=express-underground-belt] at the top are only needed, if you want to do vertical tiling.\n* Connect output.\n* Have one [item=pentapod-egg] in logistic network, or place in the [entity=requester-chest] on the right\n* Either put 250 [item=spoilage] into the [entity=assembling-machine-2] **or**\n* put ~20 [item=nutrients] anywhere on the belt\n\nFirst, the yumako mash and jelly production should start, then the bioflux and then the production of nutrients. Only after enough nutrients are available, the production of eggs and science packs will be started. \n\nIt takes several minutes, until all the items have been distributed equally throughout the factory and full production speed is reached.\n\n# Features\n\n##### Basic\n\n* Only basic Gleba buildings are used\n* No modules in blueprint, possible to add later\n* No green belts necessary\n\n##### Tileable, Compact\n\n* Blueprint can be tiled horizontally and vertically.\n* Space efficient\n* Resources are passed through top to bottom\n* Output [item=agricultural-science-pack]  are passed through to the left\n* A [entity=roboport] can be put in place of the [entity=assembling-machine-2]  (sacrificing bootstraping from spoilage capability)\n\n##### Safe\n\n* If supply of [item=jellynut] or [item=yumako] is interrupted, a safety shutdown will occur.\n* If [item=agricultural-science-pack] are backing up on the output belt, a safety shutdown will occur.\n* The biochambers will not produce more [item=pentapod-egg] than are consumed.\n* During a safety shutdown, biochambers will eject all [item=pentapod-egg] onto the belt and the heating tower will incinerate them.\n* One biochamber will not shutdown and keep eggs for later startup, but if not fed in time, the eggs will expire.\n* Laser turrets can handle some [entity=big-wriggler-pentapod-premature] from expired [item=pentapod-egg]\n\n\n##### No Waste\n\n* Close to optimal usage of resources\n* The ratios of the biochambers match the item production speeds\n* Monitoring of item quantities on the sushi belt\n\n##### Direct insertion\n\n* The most produced item, 90/s of [item=nutrients] , is directly inserted into the [item=pentapod-egg] biochambers where possible.\n* No belting of [item=yumako-mash] and [item=jelly]. They are directly inserted into the [item=bioflux] biochamber.\n\n##### Bootstrapping\n\n* Production can be bootstrapped from ~250 [item=spoilage] and one [item=pentapod-egg]\n* If a safety shutdown happens, that amount of [item=spoilage] is kept on the belt to start back up later\n\n##### Removal of excess \n\n* Keeps the sushi belt running\n* Pieces of [item=wood], that may have been put on the belt when extending the farms, are incinerated\n* When the provider chests for [item=yumako-seed] and [item=jellynut-seed] are full, extra seeds are incinerated\n* Spoilage is burned\n* During a safety shutdown, [item=pentapod-egg] are incinerated",
